<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Kyung Dong applies for listing.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Kyung Dong applies for listing.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Securities and Exchange Commission said on Friday that Kyung Dong City Gas Co had applied to be listed on the Korea Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Kyung Dong, a gas utility, has applied to list 720,000 shares at a price of 29,000 won per share.</p>
<p>Coryo Securities was the lead underwriter for the initial public offering, a statement from the commission said.</p>
<p>A commission official said schedules for subscription and listing would be announced later.</p>
<p>Kyung Dong is currently capitalised at 8.4 billion won.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
